WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.240
Whether these actors left fans behind during the&nbsp;
franchise or after it had concluded, these losses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.840
still left Harry Potter fans devastated. From&nbsp;
Potions masters to Ministry officials to magical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.160
creatures, here's a list of Harry Potter&nbsp;
cast members you may not know passed away.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.000
As soon as Harry Potter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.640
arrives at his new home at Hogwarts School of&nbsp;
Witchcraft and Wizardry, he meets his professors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.360
immediately clashing with the school's Potions&nbsp;
master, Severus Snape. Throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.360
Snape unfairly antagonizes Harry&nbsp;
and his friends, deducting points&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.440
over small mistakes and squabbles and&nbsp;
favoring students from Slytherin House.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:43.840
"Mr. Potter, our new celebrity."

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.560
The pair's animosity only gets worse when&nbsp;
Snape is forced to try to teach Harry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.040
the art of Occlumency, which could help&nbsp;
Harry block his mind against Voldemort.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:00.960
"Your lessons are at an end. Get out."

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.880
However, as it turns out, Snape was helping&nbsp;
Harry all along. As a childhood friend of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.880
Harry's mother Lily, Snape was always in&nbsp;
love with her, and he pretended to serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.960
Voldemort while reporting to Dumbledore,&nbsp;
risking his life as a double-agent.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.000
Alan Rickman was the perfect choice to play the&nbsp;
enigmatic Snape, who turns out to be one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.480
series' most complex characters. Rickman&nbsp;
brought this character to life, becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:28.400
a beloved figure to millions of Potter fans. In&nbsp;
2016, Rickman lost his life to pancreatic cancer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.960
and fans, fellow actors, and co-stars&nbsp;
alike paid their tributes to Rickman.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.160
The role of Albus Dumbledore, Harry's&nbsp;
wizened, caring mentor throughout the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.320
required an actor with enough gravitas&nbsp;
and heart to bring this part to life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.640
and for the first two Harry Potter films,&nbsp;
Richard Harris played the character to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:52.640
absolute perfection. A gentle giant whose kindness&nbsp;
is never diminished by his incredible power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.640
Dumbledore serves as Harry's makeshift&nbsp;
father figure and personal teacher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.520
sharing his boundless wisdom with Harry as he&nbsp;
gets older. However, when Dumbledore dies at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.400
end of the sixth installment, Harry Potter and&nbsp;
the Half-Blood Prince, Harry must go it alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:12.000
armed only with the lessons Dumbledore taught him&nbsp;
along the way as he sets out to defeat Voldemort.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.120
Dumbledore doesn't lose his&nbsp;
life until the sixth film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.640
but unfortunately, audiences lost the first&nbsp;
Dumbledore after only the second installment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.280
After making two Potter films, Harris was&nbsp;
diagnosed with Hodgkins' disease in 2002,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.240
and after he was hospitalized with pneumonia,&nbsp;
he died in a London hospital. Michael Gambon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.960
moved forward with the role of Dumbledore, but&nbsp;
Harris' legacy lives on through his sons — one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.240
of whom is the acclaimed actor Jared Harris, who&nbsp;
has appeared in shows like Mad Men and Chernobyl.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.480
Harry Potter faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.400
plenty of hardship throughout his&nbsp;
life, and in his pre-Hogwarts years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:52.080
most of that turmoil is caused by the Dursleys,&nbsp;
a trio of extended family members with whom Harry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.520
spends an incredibly unhappy childhood. After his&nbsp;
parents are killed by Voldemort, Harry must live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.800
with his mother's sister, Petunia, her awful&nbsp;
husband Vernon, and their dreadful son Dudley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:08.080
all of whom hate Harry for his magical ability&nbsp;
and make his life as miserable as possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.200
Despite the fact that Harry and the Dursleys hate&nbsp;
each other equally, Harry must return to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.840
house every summer when Hogwarts is on break,&nbsp;
making them important characters in the story.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:24.800
"Any funny business, any at all, and&nbsp;
you won't have any meals for a week."

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.800
As such, when it came time to cast the Dursleys,&nbsp;
producers saw fit to cast Fiona Shaw and Richard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.760
Griffiths, two titans of the British stage and&nbsp;
screen, as Petunia and Vernon, respectively.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.360
In addition to working on the Potter films,&nbsp;
Griffiths teamed up with Daniel Radcliffe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:46.800
to appear onstage in Equus from 2007-2009 on both&nbsp;
London's West End and Broadway, but unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.000
their working relationship was cut too short far&nbsp;
too soon. Griffiths lost his life to complications&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.520
from heart surgery in 2013. After losing his&nbsp;
friend and co-star, Radcliffe led a touching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.000
tribute to the legendary actor, saying he&nbsp;
was, quote, "proud" to say he knew him.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.160
Plenty of legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:09.280
actors appeared in the Harry Potter film series,&nbsp;
and few were more well-renowned than John Hurt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:14.880
As Harry goes shopping in Diagon Alley, he meets&nbsp;
the mysterious, enigmatic Ollivander, the man who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:20.560
provides wands to the entire magical community and&nbsp;
tells him an important secret about his own wand.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.560
"I wondered when I'd be seeing you, Mr. Potter."

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.440
Thanks to a magical bond between Harry and&nbsp;
Voldemort, the wand that has chosen the young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.800
wizard shares a core with Voldemort's, creating a&nbsp;
lifelong connection. Later, Ollivander must help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.360
Harry uncover the secrets of the Elder Wand&nbsp;
in order to stop Voldemort once and for all.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.960
Hurt played Ollivander in a handful&nbsp;
of Potter films, including the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.840
and last, but you might also recognize&nbsp;
this stalwart actor from V for Vendetta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.080
and Indiana Jones, as well as a short&nbsp;
stint as the War Doctor on Doctor Who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:58.080
and more. Hurt became a Knight of the Order of&nbsp;
the British Empire in 2015 for services to drama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:04.240
but sadly, he passed away only a few years later&nbsp;
in 2017 from complications from pancreatic cancer.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.280
After Harry is officially introduced&nbsp;
to the magical world by Rubeus Hagrid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.240
his first official entry into wizardry is when&nbsp;
Hagrid takes him to Diagon Alley, the magical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:19.200
street where witches and wizards can buy all of&nbsp;
the supplies they need for spells, potion-making,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.480
and more. In an otherwise non-descript Muggle&nbsp;
street in London, Harry discovers the Leaky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.760
Cauldron — a pub that seems to go totally&nbsp;
unnoticed by any non-magical folk — and in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:35.440
backyard, wizards can gain entry into Diagon Alley&nbsp;
by tapping a specific combination of bricks on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.000
wall. As the bartender of the Leaky Cauldron,&nbsp;
Tom is an important background character.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.600
"Bless my soul! It's Harry Potter!"

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:49.280
Tom only appeared briefly in the film series, but&nbsp;
in the first film, he was played by British actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.000
Derek Deadman. Throughout his career, Deadman&nbsp;
appeared in a variety of high-profile projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.400
including A Streetcar named Desirée in 1991.&nbsp;
Deadman passed away in 2014 at the age of 74&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.640
from complications from diabetes, leaving&nbsp;
the Leaky Cauldron permanently unmanned.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.080
Of course, the world of Harry Potter&nbsp;
isn't all heroes: Voldemort has plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.640
of bad guys under his thumb, one of whom&nbsp;
is the dangerous werewolf Fenrir Greyback.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:20.400
A ruthless and hungry monster, Greyback bites&nbsp;
for fun to create a new army of werewolves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.840
During Half-Blood Prince, Greyback attacks the&nbsp;
eldest Weasley son, Bill, dealing a devastating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.560
blow to Harry and his loved ones, but he's&nbsp;
ultimately taken down by the good guys.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:36.080
Greyback required a particularly imposing&nbsp;
actor, and Dave Legeno was up to the task.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.240
A trained mixed martial artist proficient&nbsp;
in everything from muay thai to judo to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:45.280
boxing to Brazilian ju-jitsu. Legeno passed&nbsp;
away in 2014 during a hike in Death Valley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.080
reportedly from problems&nbsp;
caused by the extreme heat.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.960
In the franchise's fourth installment,

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.920
Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire, Harry finds&nbsp;
himself faced with an entirely new challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:59.840
After his name is somehow placed in the&nbsp;
champion-choosing Goblet of Fire for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.120
multi-school Triwizard Tournament, Harry must&nbsp;
compete, much to everyone's chagrin. Throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:10.320
the tournament, he encounters Barty Crouch Sr., a&nbsp;
strict, high-ranking Ministry director overseeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.120
the operations of the tournament. However, what&nbsp;
Harry learns later about Crouch is that he has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:20.720
tragic past — his son, Barty Crouch Jr., played&nbsp;
by David Tennant, was previously arrested with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.400
a group of Death Eaters, and he has returned with&nbsp;
Voldemort's help to exact revenge upon his father.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.960
Since Barty Crouch Sr. is such an established&nbsp;
member of the Ministry, it stands to reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:35.600
that a venerated actor like Roger Lloyd Pack&nbsp;
would be the one to play him. Pack worked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.320
extensively on British television before he&nbsp;
passed away from pancreatic cancer in 2014.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:45.840
When it comes to magical creatures in the&nbsp;
Harry Potter universe, few are more mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:50.960
than house elves. This subservient species&nbsp;
tends to attach itself to a certain family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:55.440
performing cooking, cleaning… whatever&nbsp;
their master asks. However, Harry ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:59.280
up with much more than he bargained&nbsp;
for when he ends up owning Kreacher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:04.720
a surly house elf who once belonged to his late&nbsp;
godfather, Sirius Black. After Sirius' death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:08.800
Harry inherited ownership of Kreacher,&nbsp;
but it took Kreacher time to warm to him.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.160
Visually, Kreacher was an entirely&nbsp;
computer-generated character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.320
but he was voiced by Timothy Bateson,&nbsp;
an established British voice actor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.560
Voicing Kreacher in the fifth movie, Order of&nbsp;
the Phoenix, was Bateson's last role before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.840
he passed away in 2009; for the rest of the&nbsp;
series, Kreacher was voiced by Simon McBurney.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:31.440
As Harry enters Diagon Alley for the first&nbsp;
time, one of his first stops is Gringotts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.920
the vast wizarding bank that holds some of the&nbsp;
magical world's most closely held treasures and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:41.360
secrets. Just to add to its mystique, Gringotts&nbsp;
is guarded by goblins, which are easily the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:45.760
secretive and cryptic magical creatures in&nbsp;
Harry's world, and one of the first goblins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:50.800
Harry meets is Griphook, who leads him down&nbsp;
into Gringotts' dark and well-guarded vaults.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.040
Though Griphook returns in later films, he's&nbsp;
played by a different actor as the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.200
continues; in the first movie, Verne&nbsp;
Troyer portrays the prominent goblin.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.920
"And does Mr. Harry Potter have his key?"

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.840
Troyer has a fairly extensive film and&nbsp;
television resumé, but most people likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:14.400
know him best as Mini-Me to Mike Myers'&nbsp;
Dr. Evil in the Austin Powers franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.840
Tragically, Troyer passed away in 2018. His&nbsp;
death was later ruled a suicide. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:24.640
his performances in everything from Harry&nbsp;
Potter to Austin Powers will live on forever.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.600
When Harry arrives at Hogwarts, the&nbsp;
magic within the school astounds him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:34.800
Food appears on tables as if by magic, he&nbsp;
can wave a wand and make anything happen, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:40.320
staircases change frequently, and in an unnerving&nbsp;
twist, the paintings on the walls move and talk.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:45.280
One of those paintings, the Fat Lady, is in charge&nbsp;
of guarding the entrance to Gryffindor Tower, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:50.160
in the films, she was played by British actress&nbsp;
Elizabeth Spriggs. A Shakespearean actress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:55.520
Spriggs only made an appearance in the first film&nbsp;
before her untimely death in 2008. Dawn French&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:00.240
replaced Spriggs as the Fat Lady, popping up in&nbsp;
2004's Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban.

